            <div xml:id="d539">

                <pb facs="0691" n="592" sameAs="frus:frus1936v02/pg592"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">852.00/4014: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Italy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Phillips</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Rome</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-12-07T18:00:00+01:00">December 7, 1936—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 7—3:30 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>511. I have been informed in strictest confidence that the British and French
                    Governments having become seriously alarmed over the Spanish situation have
                    addressed a joint communication to the German, Italian, Soviet and Portuguese
                    Governments urging them to take definite steps to put a stop to the shipment of
                    arms and ammunitions to Spain. In the same communication the two Governments
                    suggested mediation between the opposing forces. My informant continued that
                    these proposals had been discussed with Ciano who had evidently not received
                    them favorably and had raised a question as to how it would be possible to
                    mediate or arbitrate in the present situation since the division of Spain
                    between the Franco and Valencia forces could scarcely constitute a solution.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
